{
    // FI_Standard_FractionalVault.ergo - one FI bond unit held for N shares, with its coupons
    // Author: CannonQ (2026)
    //
    // ZC_Standard_FractionalVault for a bond that pays coupons. Such a bond pays each coupon into
    // a coupon pool (FI_Standard_CouponVault) that the holder of its circulating unit collects.
    // Genuine vaults are created only by FI_Standard_FractionalMint compiled with
    // CONST_FRACTIONAL_VAULT_HASH = blake2b256 of this script, the only supported creator
    // (ZC_Standard_FractionalMint does not carry its stamp, age and value rules). Holds one
    // circulating bond unit on behalf of N shares, takes in the pools paid to that unit while it
    // holds it, pulls the bond's settlement (with any pools still open) out of
    // ZC_Standard_BondVault, and pays share holders pro rata.
    //
    // CONSTANTS
    // CONST_COUPON_VAULT_HASH: Coll[Byte] - blake2b256 of FI_Standard_CouponVault, the coupon pool
    // CONST_REPAYMENT_TOKEN: Coll[Byte] - the bond's repayment token id; empty for an ERG bond.
    //   Coupons are counted in this token only, so one vault, and so one mint, per repayment
    //   asset. A unit of a bond repaid in another token can be deposited, but its token coupons
    //   cannot be taken in.
    //
    // TOKENS
    // tokens(0): (share, N+1) - the reserve, kept through every transition and burned only by the
    //   final claim. Supply is 2*N+1, so for a known (share, N) the box holding N+1 units is the
    //   share's state box: found by token id, authenticated by amount, usable as a data input.
    // tokens(1..): before the pull (bond asset, 1), then (repayment token, coupons) once any are
    //   taken in, and no other token. After it, (repayment token, coupons plus proceeds) if any,
    //   then the settlement proceeds' other tokens in their order.
    //
    // REGISTERS
    // R4: Coll[Byte] - bond asset id
    // R5: Coll[Long] - (N, outstanding shares, pull fee). Outstanding starts at N and falls with
    //   each claim. The pull fee was funded into this box's value at mint: at least 0.1 ERG through
    //   FI_Standard_FractionalMint. This script itself enforces no minimum.
    // R6: Byte - bond settlement path, 0 repaid / 1 liquidated. Present only after the pull.
    // State is read from the tokens: the vault is "holding" while tokens(1..) holds the bond asset.
    // ERG coupons are part of the value.
    //
    // PATHS. Context var 9 selects REFRESH; otherwise the shares burned select the path, where
    // burned = transaction-wide share inputs minus share outputs.
    // ABSORB OR PULL (burned = 0, holding; anyone). Context var 0: Int successor index.
    //   The pools are all inputs at the coupon pool script; each must have R4 = the bond asset.
    //   The caller's cut is 1/200 (0.5%), rounded down, of what the pools bring: of their summed
    //   nanoERG, and of their summed repayment token. It is reckoned on the pools alone, never on
    //   this box or the bond vault, so a pool made by hand returns at most 0.5% of itself and
    //   takes nothing of what this box held. A pool of under 200 units yields no cut.
    //   The successor keeps this script, R4, R5 and the reserve, is created at HEIGHT - 999 or
    //   later and has no R7. Its value is at least this box's
    //   plus every pool's (and, at a pull, the bond vault's, less the pull fee), less the nanoERG
    //   cut. Its coupon entry (repayment token, c) is there when c > 0, where c is the repayment
    //   token summed over this box, the pools and the bond vault, less the token cut. Successor
    //   tokens are exact given the cut, and each pool's own rule asks for every token it holds in
    //   the successor, less the same cut, so a pool holding any other token cannot be taken in.
    // ABSORB (no other input holds the bond asset; at least one pool). Successor tokens: the
    //   reserve, (bond asset, 1), then the coupon entry; no R6. The caller keeps the cut and pays
    //   the miner fee from its own inputs.
    // PULL (one other input holds the bond asset; pools optional). That input is the settled
    //   ZC_Standard_BondVault: only it can hold the other 2 units, at tokens(0). It must have been
    //   created at least 720 blocks before HEIGHT: FI_Standard_Bond stamps it within 15 blocks of
    //   its settlement, so every pool has about 720 blocks to be absorbed first. The bond vault's
    //   refresh re-stamps it, which can only restart and so lengthen the wait. All 3 bond units
    //   are burned. Successor tokens: the reserve, the coupon entry, then the bond vault's
    //   tokens(1..) other than the repayment token, in order; R6 = the bond vault's path. The
    //   puller keeps up to the pull fee R5(2) out of the combined value, plus the cut when pools
    //   are in, so taking pools in never pays less than leaving them out. The pools' rule lets a
    //   3-unit burn at a contract home keep the smaller of the home's R5(2) and the home's own
    //   value, and the cut, out of its payout.
    // PARTIAL CLAIM (0 < burned < outstanding, after the pull only).
    //   Context var 0: Int continuation index; 1: Int payout index, distinct.
    //   Pays floor(balance * burned / outstanding) of nanoERG and of EACH token; the rest stays
    //   under this script with outstanding reduced, in a continuation created at HEIGHT - 999 or
    //   later with R6 kept and no R7. Products use BigInt before division.
    // FINAL CLAIM (burned = outstanding + N + 1). Context var 1: Int payout index.
    //   Every outstanding share AND the reserve are burned; the payout takes everything. Before
    //   the pull this returns the bond unit and every coupon taken in: holding all shares
    //   un-fractionalizes the bond.
    // Payout outputs carry R4 = SELF.id, so one output cannot serve two vaults.
    // REFRESH (context var 9 present; anyone, once the box is more than 525600 blocks, about two
    //   years, old). Var 9: Int successor index. Storage rent lets anyone take a four-year-old box
    //   whose value does not cover the rent, tokens included, which would free the share reserve
    //   and the bond unit. So anyone may re-create the box to reset its age, keeping up to
    //   10000000 nanoERG (0.01 ERG) as a bounty. It never takes the value below 1000000, plus
    //   the pull fee while the bond unit is still held; a box at or under that is renewed for
    //   nothing, and a vault from FI_Standard_FractionalMint starts exactly there. The successor
    //   has this script, the same tokens and registers and no more, and a creation height within
    //   1000 blocks of HEIGHT (up to HEIGHT itself). No shares may be burned in the transaction.
    //   The age and the bounty are ZC_Standard_Bond's; its successor stamp window is not.
    //
    // ASSUMPTIONS AND LIMITS
    // - Coupons reach share holders only through the claims, after the pull pro rata to shares
    //   burned, or all at once by a final claim before it. A holder who sells shares before the
    //   pull sells their part of the coupons too.
    // - Once the pull burns the unit no pool of the bond can be collected. A pool neither taken in
    //   nor spent in the pull has no collector: the borrower, the puller and the share holders
    //   cannot take it, and it stays unspendable except by a refresh that re-creates it. Nothing
    //   here can tell that a pool was left out. Whoever sends the absorb or pull keeps the cut on
    //   the pools it includes, which is the incentive to include them all (a pool under 200
    //   units pays no cut). Builders must find and include every unspent pool of the bond whose
    //   tokens are the repayment token or none; a pool holding any other token makes the
    //   transaction fail. A vault 1051200 or more blocks old must be refreshed before an absorb
    //   or pull that carries pools: the pools accept no home that old.
    // - Share holders pay the cut, out of the coupons. ABSORB and the claims are never delayed; a
    //   final claim before the pull takes the unit and every coupon taken in.
    // - The vault cannot tell a genuine pool from a box made by hand at the pool script naming the
    //   bond. Such a box adds only nanoERG and the repayment token, or cannot be taken; but any
    //   absorb spends this box and voids a claim or pull built on it, to be rebuilt.
    // - Before the pull the box holds at most three tokens. After it the reserve stands in for the
    //   bond vault's 2 units and its repayment token is merged into the coupon entry, which adds
    //   one entry only when the bond vault held none. The successor must fit the node's box size
    //   limit for the pull to go through.
    // - N is free and unrelated to the proceeds' raw units, so a small claim can round to zero for
    //   an asset. Rounding dust stays for later claimants; the final claim takes it all.
    // - Claimants fund fees and minimum-box top-ups. Payouts and continuations may receive extra
    //   ERG; tokens are exact. Claims on one vault serialize; different vaults may share a
    //   transaction that takes in no pools (each pool input must name this bond, and the pools'
    //   rule counts every input at this script toward this box's successor).
    // - The payout destination is chosen by whoever supplies the shares. Joint claimants must
    //   agree.
    // - The proceeds are assumed not to contain this vault's own share token: the bond's
    //   collateral is fixed before the share id exists. A liquidation expression that injects it
    //   is unsupported.
    // - Shares lost or burned outside these paths strand their entitlement. No sweep authority.
    // - A hand-made box with this script cannot hold a genuine reserve; see
    //   FI_Standard_FractionalMint for share verification. Anyone can create and spend a box at
    //   this script (a self-minted reserve passes the final claim), so it must never be named as
    //   an owner or borrower script. A refresh relies on someone sending it within the two years
    //   before rent is due.
    // - Storage rent after maturity: FI_Standard_Order caps a bond's life at 788400 blocks, so a
    //   vault minted near the bond's start and never absorbed reaches the rent age (1051200
    //   blocks) about 262800 blocks after a full-life maturity. Taken whole before the pull, it
    //   frees its unit, and with it the settlement and the pools. A rent fee that leaves less
    //   than the pull fee in the box blocks the pull.

    def numTokenInInputs(tokenId: Coll[Byte]): Long = {
        INPUTS.fold(0L, { (a: Long, b: Box) =>
            val count = b.tokens.fold(0L, { (z: Long, t: (Coll[Byte], Long)) =>
                if (t._1 == tokenId) z + t._2 else z
            })
            a + count
        })
    }

    def numTokenInOutputs(tokenId: Coll[Byte]): Long = {
        OUTPUTS.fold(0L, { (a: Long, b: Box) =>
            val count = b.tokens.fold(0L, { (z: Long, t: (Coll[Byte], Long)) =>
                if (t._1 == tokenId) z + t._2 else z
            })
            a + count
        })
    }

    val shareId = SELF.tokens(0)._1
    val reserve = SELF.tokens(0)._2
    val bondAsset = SELF.R4[Coll[Byte]].get
    val supply = SELF.R5[Coll[Long]].get
    val assets = SELF.tokens.slice(1, SELF.tokens.size)
    val holding = assets.exists { (t: (Coll[Byte], Long)) => t._1 == bondAsset }
    val burned = numTokenInInputs(shareId) - numTokenInOutputs(shareId)

    if (supply.size != 3 || supply(0) < 1L || supply(0) > 1000000000L || reserve != supply(0) + 1L ||
        supply(1) < 1L || supply(1) > supply(0) || burned < 0L) {
        sigmaProp(false)
    } else {
        val outstanding = supply(1)
        val refreshIndex = getVar[Int](9)

        if (refreshIndex.isDefined) {
            // Refresh: re-create the box unchanged to reset its age, paying the refresher.
            val index = refreshIndex.get
            if (index < 0 || index >= OUTPUTS.size) {
                sigmaProp(false)
            } else {
                val next = OUTPUTS(index)
                val stamped = next.creationInfo._1
                // A holding vault keeps its pull fee, so the pull can still pay its batcher.
                val floor = if (holding) 1000000L + supply(2) else 1000000L
                val kept = if (SELF.value < floor) SELF.value else floor
                val least = if (SELF.value - 10000000L > kept) SELF.value - 10000000L else kept
                // R6 exists only after the pull; the successor keeps it as it is.
                val pathKept = if (SELF.R6[Byte].isDefined) {
                    next.R6[Byte].get == SELF.R6[Byte].get && next.R7[Coll[Byte]].isDefined == false
                } else next.R6[Byte].isDefined == false
                sigmaProp(
                    burned == 0L &&
                    SELF.creationInfo._1 < HEIGHT - 525600 &&
                    stamped > HEIGHT - 1000 && stamped <= HEIGHT &&
                    next.propositionBytes == SELF.propositionBytes &&
                    next.value >= least &&
                    next.tokens == SELF.tokens &&
                    next.R4[Coll[Byte]].get == bondAsset &&
                    next.R5[Coll[Long]].get == supply &&
                    pathKept
                )
            }
        } else if (burned == 0L) {
            // Absorb coupon pools into this box, or pull the settled bond vault (and any pools)
            val nextIndex = getVar[Int](0).get
            val sources = INPUTS.filter { (b: Box) =>
                b.id != SELF.id && b.tokens.exists { (t: (Coll[Byte], Long)) => t._1 == bondAsset }
            }
            val pullFee = supply(2)
            if (!holding || sources.size > 1 || pullFee < 0L || pullFee > SELF.value ||
                nextIndex < 0 || nextIndex >= OUTPUTS.size) {
                sigmaProp(false)
            } else {
                val next = OUTPUTS(nextIndex)
                val coupon = CONST_REPAYMENT_TOKEN
                val pools = INPUTS.filter { (b: Box) => blake2b256(b.propositionBytes) == CONST_COUPON_VAULT_HASH }
                // What joins this box: the settled bond vault, at a pull, and the pools.
                val parts = sources.append(pools)
                val inCoupon = { (b: Box) =>
                    b.tokens.fold(0L, { (z: Long, u: (Coll[Byte], Long)) => if (u._1 == coupon) z + u._2 else z })
                }
                // The caller's cut: 1/200 of the pools' own nanoERG and repayment token, rounded down.
                val pooledErg = pools.fold(0L, { (a: Long, b: Box) => a + b.value })
                val pooledCoupons = pools.fold(0L, { (a: Long, b: Box) => a + inCoupon(b) })
                val coupons = parts.fold(inCoupon(SELF) - pooledCoupons / 200L, { (a: Long, b: Box) => a + inCoupon(b) })
                val erg = parts.fold(SELF.value - pullFee * sources.size.toLong - pooledErg / 200L,
                    { (a: Long, b: Box) => a + b.value })
                // The settled bond vault's tokens after its 2 units; none at an absorb. In the
                // successor below, slice(0, 2 - sources.size) keeps the reserve and, at an absorb
                // only, the bond unit; SELF's own coupons re-enter through the summed entry.
                val proceeds = sources.fold(SELF.tokens.slice(0, 0), { (a: Coll[(Coll[Byte], Long)], b: Box) =>
                    b.tokens.slice(1, b.tokens.size)
                })
                sigmaProp(
                    parts.size > 0 &&
                    next.propositionBytes == SELF.propositionBytes &&
                    next.creationInfo._1 > HEIGHT - 1000 &&
                    next.R7[Coll[Byte]].isDefined == false &&
                    next.R4[Coll[Byte]].get == bondAsset &&
                    next.R5[Coll[Long]].get == supply &&
                    pools.forall { (b: Box) => b.R4[Coll[Byte]].get == bondAsset } &&
                    next.value >= erg &&
                    next.tokens == SELF.tokens.slice(0, 2 - sources.size)
                        .append(Coll((coupon, coupons)).filter { (t: (Coll[Byte], Long)) => t._2 > 0L })
                        .append(proceeds.filter { (t: (Coll[Byte], Long)) => t._1 != coupon }) &&
                    next.R6[Byte].isDefined == (sources.size == 1) &&
                    sources.forall { (b: Box) =>
                        b.tokens(0)._1 == bondAsset && numTokenInOutputs(bondAsset) == 0L &&
                        next.R6[Byte].get == b.R5[Byte].get && HEIGHT >= b.creationInfo._1 + 720
                    }
                )
            }
        } else {
            val payoutIndex = getVar[Int](1).get
            if (payoutIndex < 0 || payoutIndex >= OUTPUTS.size) {
                sigmaProp(false)
            } else {
                val payout = OUTPUTS(payoutIndex)
                val payoutTagged = payout.R4[Coll[Byte]].get == SELF.id

                if (burned == outstanding + reserve) {
                    // Final claim: all outstanding shares and the reserve are gone
                    sigmaProp(payoutTagged && payout.value >= SELF.value && payout.tokens == assets)
                } else {
                    val nextIndex = getVar[Int](0).get
                    if (holding || burned >= outstanding ||
                        nextIndex < 0 || nextIndex >= OUTPUTS.size || nextIndex == payoutIndex) {
                        sigmaProp(false)
                    } else {
                        val next = OUTPUTS(nextIndex)
                        val paidERG = (SELF.value.toBigInt * burned.toBigInt / outstanding.toBigInt).toLong
                        val paidTokens = assets.map { (t: (Coll[Byte], Long)) =>
                            (t._1, (t._2.toBigInt * burned.toBigInt / outstanding.toBigInt).toLong)
                        }.filter { (t: (Coll[Byte], Long)) => t._2 > 0L }
                        val retainedTokens = assets.map { (t: (Coll[Byte], Long)) =>
                            (t._1, t._2 - (t._2.toBigInt * burned.toBigInt / outstanding.toBigInt).toLong)
                        }.filter { (t: (Coll[Byte], Long)) => t._2 > 0L }

                        val paid = payoutTagged && payout.value >= paidERG && payout.tokens == paidTokens
                        val continued =
                            next.propositionBytes == SELF.propositionBytes &&
                            next.creationInfo._1 > HEIGHT - 1000 &&
                            next.R7[Coll[Byte]].isDefined == false &&
                            next.value >= SELF.value - paidERG &&
                            next.tokens == SELF.tokens.slice(0, 1).append(retainedTokens) &&
                            next.R4[Coll[Byte]].get == bondAsset &&
                            next.R5[Coll[Long]].get == Coll(supply(0), outstanding - burned, supply(2)) &&
                            next.R6[Byte].get == SELF.R6[Byte].get

                        sigmaProp(paid && continued)
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
